{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work-list", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"facets": {}, "total-results": 1380137, "items": [{"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2024, 5, 13]], "date-time": "2024-05-13T20:22:18Z", "timestamp": 1715631738128}, "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "Edinburgh University Press", "isbn-type": [{"value": "9781399503815", "type": "print"}, {"value": "9781399503839", "type": "electronic"}], "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "published-print": {"date-parts": [[2022, 8, 2]]}, "abstract": "<p>This chapter reviews the emergence of golf societies in the mid-eighteenth century and discusses the contentious issue of the relative antiquity of early Scottish and English golf societies. In addition, the emergence of women's golf is discussed. There is very little evidence of golf having been played by women prior to the nineteenth century and the earliest identified evidence of women playing golf in the eighteenth century is a newspaper article from 1738 concerning women playing golf on Bruntsfield Links. In contrast, claims relating to golf being played by Catherine of Aragon (1513) and the Countess of Mar (1638) can be dismissed and claims relating to Mary Queen of Scots (1542\u201387) have been shown to be either incorrect or questionable.</p>", "DOI": "10.3366/edinburgh/9781399503815.003.0015", "type": "book-chapter", "created": {"date-parts": [[2023, 9, 22]], "date-time": "2023-09-22T09:38:10Z", "timestamp": 1695375490000}, "page": "153-162", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["Early Golf Societies and Early Women\u2019s Golf"], "prefix": "10.3366", "author": [{"given": "Neil S.", "family": "Millar", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "1931", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2023, 9, 21]]}, "container-title": ["Early Golf"], "original-title": ["Early Golf Societies and Early Women\u2019s Golf"], "language": "en", "deposited": {"date-parts": [[2023, 9, 22]], "date-time": "2023-09-22T09:38:10Z", "timestamp": 1695375490000}, "score": 8.803921, "resource": {"primary": {"URL": "https://academic.oup.com/edinburgh-scholarship-online/book/51603/chapter/418235479"}}, "issued": {"date-parts": [[2022, 8, 2]]}, "ISBN": ["9781399503815", "9781399503839"], "references-count": 0, "URL": "https://doi.org/10.3366/edinburgh/9781399503815.003.0015", "published": {"date-parts": [[2022, 8, 2]]}}, {"institution": [{"name": "European Space Agency", "acronym": ["ESA"], "department": ["D/SCI"]}], "indexed": {"date-parts": [[2022, 3, 30]], "date-time": "2022-03-30T14:26:51Z", "timestamp": 1648650411558}, "description": "the aim of this proposal is to study starbursts in cluster environments at epochs close to their formation. it is based on the increasing evidence that elliptical galaxies went through an infrared luminous phase at redshifts of z = 2-5 comma  and the expectation that infrared quasars at high redshifts are in rich protoclusters. in this context comma  we propose a 10x10 arc min deep survey with cam and phot in the direction of high redshift objects known to have large mass contents of dust and-or molecular gas.  as a second priority we propose a search for infrared luminous objects in high redshift superclusters by mapping a larger area of 1 degree square around one of the first priority targets.", "reference-count": 0, "publisher": "European Space Agency", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "DOI": "10.5270/esa-yiziu2m", "type": "dataset", "created": {"date-parts": [[2021, 2, 1]], "date-time": "2021-02-01T11:54:03Z", "timestamp": 1612180443000}, "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 0, "title": ["EARLY"], "prefix": "10.5270", "author": [{"name": "European Space Agency", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"role": "author", "vocabulary": "crossref"}]}], "member": "3228", "container-title": ["EARLY"], "deposited": {"date-parts": [[